.TH RUN-APPOWNERS 1 "2026-11-03" "cti-agent 1.4" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
run-appowners \- daily: mail each application's scanner report to its owners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run\-appowners
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-to\-dev ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent run\-appowners
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-to\-dev ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B run-appowners
sends each application's Qualys WAS report of open findings, with the scan
account's session removed, to the owner and watchers on that application's
line in
.IR app\-owners.txt ,
the morning after the scan finishes. Many of them are outside the company and
not in Jira, which is why this is email and not a ticket.
.PP
It is run by
.B cti\-agent\-appowners.service
from
.B cti\-agent\-appowners.timer
daily at 07:15
.RB ( Persistent=true ).
With
.B OWNER_ALLOW_DOMAINS
unset it logs that the lane is off and exits 0, except on
.BR \-\-to\-dev .
.PP
The steps, in order:
.TP
.B 1. Plan
.B cti\-appscan \-\-since 48h \-\-deliveries\-out \-\-delivered\-log
lists the scans finished since the last run and not yet sent or held. Fatal
on a non-zero exit.
.TP
.B 2. Prepare
.B cti\-appreport \-\-deliveries \-\-out\-dir
fetches, redacts and writes each email
.RB ( \-\-no\-fetch
on a dry run). Fatal on a non-zero exit.
.TP
.B 3. Send
One
.B cti\-mailer \-\-lane owner \-\-app\-id \-\-app\-name
per application, with the report attached. The mailer, not this runner,
decides the recipients (see
.BR cti\-mailer (1)).
A refused send is logged and tried again on the next run.
.TP
.B 4. Record
On a real run only,
.B cti\-appscan \-\-commit\-delivered
records each sent scan, and each held one, in
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/appowners\-sent.json ,
so each is dealt with once.
.TP
.B 5. Operator
Held scans and watchers refused for their domain go to
.BR cti\-alert (1)
as one HOLD. Never fatal.
.PP
The working directory is deleted on every way out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Plan and check every recipient through
.BR "cti\-mailer \-\-dry\-run" .
Fetches no report (a report is created in the scanner), sends, records and
alerts nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-to\-dev
Every email, with its report, to
.B FLEET_DEV_EMAIL
only, subject prefixed [DEV TEST]; the operator alert goes there too. Records
nothing, so the real run still sends. Works before
.B OWNER_ALLOW_DOMAINS
is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OWNER_ALLOW_DOMAINS
Domains an owner or watcher may be at, comma-separated and exact. Unset: the
lane is off.
.TP
.B APPSCAN_OWNERS_FILE
The owners file; default
.IR /etc/cti\-agent/app\-owners.txt .
.TP
.B FLEET_DEV_EMAIL
Where
.B \-\-to\-dev
sends.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $FLEET_HOME/state/appowners\-sent.json
Last scan sent or held per application.
.TP
.I $FLEET_HOME/state/appowners\-<stamp>/
This run's reports and emails, 0700, deleted when the run ends.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done, including when the lane is off, nothing was new, or some sends were
refused (each is logged and retried).
.TP
.B 1
A missing binary, an unknown argument,
.B \-\-to\-dev
without
.BR FLEET_DEV_EMAIL ,
or the plan or preparation step failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo cti\-agent run\-appowners \-\-dry\-run
sudo cti\-agent run\-appowners \-\-to\-dev
journalctl \-u cti\-agent\-appowners \-n 50 \-\-no\-pager
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now cti\-agent\-appowners.timer
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-appscan (1),
.BR cti\-appscan (1),
.BR cti\-appreport (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-alert (1)
